WEBVTT

00:00:00.153 --> 00:00:01.246
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Part 5

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:10.885
<v><b>William:</b></v> A line of people began trickling through the alleys from the shops and heading in my direction.

00:00:11.732 --> 00:00:16.162
They’d seen the tower from the market and were walking towards my house.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:23.982
I recognized a few of the traders…One asked, ‘What is this thing?...What does it do?’

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:32.168
‘Generates electricity from the wind. I’ll show you.’ ‘That’s impossible,’ he said…

00:00:32.755 --> 00:00:35.090
‘Stand back and watch.’…

00:00:36.855 --> 00:00:39.501
More and more people arrived…

00:00:40.514 --> 00:00:45.211
Looking out, I saw my parents and sisters at the back of the crowd.

00:00:46.155 --> 00:00:51.552
‘Let’s see how crazy this boy really is,’ said someone in the crowd.

00:00:52.605 --> 00:00:59.250
A steady wind whipped through the rungs of the tower. <i>Here it goes</i>, I thought.

00:01:00.344 --> 00:01:06.196
I grabbed the bicycle spoke and jerked it loose. The blades began to turn.

00:01:07.016 --> 00:01:13.456
…The tyre spun slowly, creaking at first. Everything was happening in slow motion.

00:01:14.309 --> 00:01:16.171
I needed it to go faster.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:22.253
<i>Come on</i>, I begged. <i>Don’t embarrass me now</i>.

00:01:23.487 --> 00:01:28.314
Slowly, the blades picked up speed. <i>Come on, come on</i>.

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:36.298
Just then a gust of wind slammed against my body, and the blades kicked up like mad.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.587
The tower rocked once, knocking me off balance.

00:01:41.461 --> 00:01:48.903
I wrapped my elbow around the wooden rung as the blades spun like furious propellers behind my head.

00:01:50.036 --> 00:01:57.511
I held the bulb before me, waiting for my miracle. It flickered once.

00:01:58.392 --> 00:02:05.164
Just a flash at first, then a surge of bright, magnificent light.

00:02:05.818 --> 00:02:12.043
My heart nearly burst. ‘Look,’ someone said. ‘He’s made light!’…

00:02:12.697 --> 00:02:17.366
It was glorious light, and it was absolutely mine!

00:02:18.952 --> 00:02:22.363
I threw my hands in the air and screamed with joy.

00:02:23.084 --> 00:02:27.354
…Dangling now by one arm with the bulb burning bright in my hand,

00:02:27.574 --> 00:02:31.915
I looked down at the eyes below, now wide in disbelief.

00:02:32.922 --> 00:02:38.335
‘Electric wind!’ I shouted. ‘I told you I wasn’t mad!’

00:02:48.097 --> 00:02:53.044
<v><b>Presenter:</b></v> William Kamkwamba first used his windmill to provide power for his home,

00:02:53.437 --> 00:03:00.374
but it was later used to pump water from the village well and enable the farmers to irrigate their crops.

00:03:01.109 --> 00:03:04.559
Since his windmill became a global news story,

00:03:04.805 --> 00:03:09.386
William has graduated from college and given acclaimed TED talks.

00:03:09.939 --> 00:03:15.942
Now 37, he designs instruction manuals to create low-cost, high-impact,

00:03:15.967 --> 00:03:20.221
easy-to-assemble projects in communities around the world.

00:03:20.972 --> 00:03:26.859
The film <i>The Boy Who Harnessed the Wind</i> is available to stream on Netflix.